hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"896","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a person supplicates, he should be abundant in his asking, for nothing is great (i.e., difficult) for Allah Almighty."
"897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A little relief appeared and they could see the sky. The second person said: O Allah! You know that I had a cousin whom I loved intensely, as men love women. Once I sought her nearness, but she said: ‘No, not until you give me one hundred dinars.’ I strove for it and gathered the amount, then came to her. When I sat between her legs, she said: ‘O servant of Allah, fear Allah and do not break the seal unlawfully.’ So I left her. O Allah! If You know that I did this hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then grant us relief and show us the sky. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A piece of the rock moved and they could see the sky. The third person said: O Allah! I hired a man for a specific measure of rice. When night came, I paid him his wages, but he did not take it and became angry with me. I took the measure of rice and started farming with it until it turned into cows and goats. After some time, that man came to me and said: ‘O servant of Allah! Fear Allah and do not wrong me in my wages.’ So I said to him: ‘Take these cows and their shepherd.’ He said: ‘Fear Allah and do not mock me.’ I said: ‘I am not mocking you. These are yours. If I wished, I could have given you only a measure of rice.’ O Allah! If You know that I did this hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then grant us relief. So the rock moved away from there and they came out.”"
"898",""" O Allah, it is unto Thee that I surrender myself. I affirm my faith in Thee and repose my trust in Thee and turn to Thee in repentance and with Thy help fought my adversaries. O Allah, I seek refuge in Thee with Thine Power; there is no god but Thou, lest Thou leadest me astray. Thou art ever-living that dieth not, while the Jinn and mankind die."" (Using translation from Muslim 2717)"
"899","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You should recite this: “O Allah! Save me from the evil of my own self and make me firm upon the most guided matter.” Then the man left. He had not accepted Islam. (After some time, he again came to your service.) He said: O Messenger of Allah! I had come to you before and requested you to teach me something, so you said: “O Allah! Save me from the evil of my own self and make me firm upon the most guided matter.” Now that I have accepted Islam, what should I say? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You should say: “O Allah! Save me from the evil of my own self and make me firm upon the most guided matter. O Allah! Forgive whatever I have done secretly or openly, whatever I have done by mistake, whatever I have done deliberately, and whatever I have done unknowingly.”"
"900","the Prophet (saas) used to say: ""Allahumma inni as'alukal-huda wat-tuqa wal-'afaf wal-ghina (O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and affluence)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3832)"
"901","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) supplicating: ""O Allah! I seek from You the most guided guidance in my affairs, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self."
"902","Verily, the hearts of all the sons of Adam are between the two fingers out of the fingers of the Compassionate Lord as one heart. He turns that to any (direction) He likes. Then Allahs Messenger ﷺ said: 0 Allah, the Turner of the hearts, turn our hearts to Thine obedience. (Using translation from Muslim 2655)"
"903","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A believer is never satisfied with doing good until his abode is Paradise."
"904","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever sends salah upon me once, Allah (SWT) will send salah upon him tenfold, and will erase ten sins from him, and will raise him ten degrees in status."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1297)"
"905","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever sends blessings upon me once, ten good deeds will be written in his record of deeds."
"906","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever sends salah upon me once, Allah (SWT) will send salah upon him tenfold."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1296)"
"907","I said Ameen. When someone finds his parents or one of them and does not treat them well, and after dying enters Hell, then may Allah (distance him from His mercy), you say Ameen, so I said Ameen. (Then Jibreel said:) Whoever hears your mention and does not send blessings upon you, and after dying enters Hell, then may Allah (distance him from His mercy), you say Ameen, so I said Ameen."
"908","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “May the nose of that person be rubbed in dust before whom my mention is made and he does not send blessings upon me. May the nose of that person be rubbed in dust who finds his parents in old age and they do not cause him to enter Paradise. May the nose of that person be rubbed in dust before whom the month of Ramadan comes and then that month passes before he is forgiven.”"
"909","narrates from his father (Sayyiduna Imam Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the miser is the one in whose presence my mention is made and he does not send blessings upon me."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the most authentic narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Imam Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him). Because at the time when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, Sayyiduna Imam Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) was one month short of seven years old. That is, he was born in the month of Sha'ban in the 4th year of Hijrah, and when he was six years and a few months old, he was memorizing many things in Arabic one after another."
"910","The Prophet ﷺ said: Among the most excellent of your days is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he died, on it the last trumpet will be blown, and on it the shout will be made, so invoke more blessings on me that day, for your blessings will be submitted to me. The people asked: Messenger of Allah, how can it be that our blessings will be submitted to you while your body is decayed? He replied: Allah, the Exalted, has prohibited the earth from consuming the bodies of Prophets. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1047)"
"911","Messenger of Allah said: ""The person closest to me on the Day of Judgement is the one who sent the most Salat upon me."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 484)"
"912","""Ka'b bin Ujrah said to me: 'Shall I not give you a gift?' We said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we know about sending salams upon you, but how should we send salah upon you?"" He said: 'Say: Alahumma salli 'ala Muhammad wa 'ala ali Muhammad, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahima wa barik 'ala Muhammad kama barakta 'ala ali Ibrahim fil-'alamin, innaka hamidun majid (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent salah upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim among the nations. You are indeed Worthy of praise, Full of glory.)'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1289)"
"913","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah writes ten good deeds for him in return."
"914","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah (SWT) has angels who travel around on Earth conveying to me the Salams of my Ummah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1282)"
"915","I will send mercy upon him ten times in return, and whoever sends peace upon you once, I will send peace upon him ten times in return? So I replied: Yes! O my Lord."
"916","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and my wife said in a loud voice in your presence: O Messenger of Allah! Please supplicate for mercy for me and my husband. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah send mercy upon you and your husband."
"917","narrates: Whenever people from a household would bring charity to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he would supplicate for mercy for them. My father presented his charity to him, so he said: O Allah! Send mercy upon the family of Abu Awfa."
"918","A woman said to the Prophet ﷺ: Invoke blessing on me as well as on my husband. The Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah send blessing on you and your husband. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1533)"
"919","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) This continues until the break of dawn."
"920","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Our Lord who is blessed and exalted descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last one-third of the night remains, and says: Who supplicated Me so that I may answer him ? Who asks of Me so that I may give to him ? Who asks My forgiveness so that I may forgive him ? (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1315)"
"921","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty waits, until when one third of the night has passed, our Lord descends towards the sky of the world. Our Lord says: Is there anyone seeking forgiveness? Is there anyone repenting? Is there anyone asking? Is there anyone supplicating? (The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) This continues until the true dawn. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Imam Malik has narrated from Zuhri, as we have mentioned, that when one third of the night remains, Allah Almighty descends. And in the narration transmitted by Abu Ishaq from Al-Agharr, it is mentioned that He descends until one third of the night has passed. So, there is a possibility in this that in some nights He descends when one third of the night remains, and in some nights He descends when the initial one third of the night has passed. In this way, there will be no difference or contradiction between the two narrations."
"922","I will grant you one of these things. ""O Allah! I ask You for Your swift well-being, or patience upon Your trial, or to depart from this world towards Your mercy."
"923","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked to supplicate three times and to ask pardon (of Allah) three times. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1524)"
"924","his grandfather said: ""The Messenger of Allah (saas) said: 'I seek the forgivenenss of Allah and repent to Him seventy times each day.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3816)"
"925","the Messenger of Allah (saas) said: 'I seek the forgiveness of Allah and repent to Him one hundred times each day.' (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3815)"
"926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then why are you neglectful of seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from Allah one hundred times every day. Abu Ishaq says: I narrated this hadith before Abu Burdah, and he said: (These words are also in the narration) ""I repent"" (that is, I repent and seek forgiveness one hundred times every day)."
"927","We counted that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say a hundred times during a meeting: ""My Lord, forgive me and pardon me; Thou art the Pardoning and forgiving One"". (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1516)"
"928","The Noble Mustafa (peace and blessings be upon him) used to seek forgiveness from his Lord in various circumstances, as we have mentioned, even though Allah Almighty had already forgiven his past and future sins. There can be two meanings to the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) seeking forgiveness. One is that Allah Almighty sent him as a teacher for his people in both word and deed, so he would invite his Ummah to seek forgiveness and to be regular in it, because he knew that his Ummah would often fall into sins. Thus, they would continue to act upon the practice of seeking forgiveness. The second meaning is that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would seek forgiveness for himself regarding any shortcoming in performing good deeds. He did not seek forgiveness from sins, because Allah Almighty kept him pure (from sins) among all His creation, and He accepted his supplication regarding the (innate) devil that is with everyone, until he became a Muslim. So, the situation is such that this was included in the character of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He would act regularly in obedience to Allah Almighty. He would not discontinue it, to the extent that sometimes, due to being engaged in another good deed, he would not be able to perform a particular good deed, and that good deed would be missed by him. Just as, due to being busy, he could not perform the two rak‘ahs after Dhuhr, because a delegation from the tribe of Tamim had come and he was distributing wealth among them and providing them with mounts. Because of this, the two rak‘ahs after Dhuhr were missed by him, so he performed them after ‘Asr. After that, he continued to perform those rak‘ahs regularly at that time. So, the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) seeking forgiveness was regarding the shortcoming in good deeds, that due to being busy, he could not perform them at their prescribed time, and he was engaged in other good deeds which, at that time, were more necessary than the ones he regularly performed. It was not that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sought forgiveness from sins that he had committed."
"929","The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), ""Repent to your Lord,"" means seek forgiveness from your Lord. Similarly, the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), ""I repent to Him one hundred times a day,"" means that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to seek forgiveness regarding any shortcoming in his good deeds, which he had set as a regular practice for himself. It was his routine that when he performed a good deed, he would maintain it and do it regularly. Sometimes, due to some engagement, he could not perform that good deed which he used to do regularly. And this would happen because of being occupied with another good deed, just as he was busy with the delegation of Banu Tamim, and due to distributing wealth among them, he could not perform the two rak‘ahs which he used to offer after Zuhr. So when he performed the ‘Asr prayer, he also performed those two rak‘ahs. Thus, the seeking of forgiveness by the Prophet (peace be upon him) was regarding the shortcoming in that good deed which he could not perform due to being occupied with another good deed, as we have mentioned earlier."
"930","the Messenger of Allah said: “Verily, when the slave (of Allah) commits a sin, a black spot appears on his heart. When he refrains from it, seeks forgiveness and repents, his heart is polished clean. But if he returns, it increases until it covers his entire heart. And that is the ‘Ran’ which Allah mentioned: ‘Nay, but on their hearts is the Ran which they used to earn.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3334)"
"931","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: My heart is invaded by unmindfulness, and I ask Allah's pardon a hundred times in the day. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1515)"
"932","The Prophet [SAW] said: ""The best of prayers for forgiveness is for a person to say: 'Allahumma, anta rabbi, la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduka, wa ana 'ala 'ahdika wa wa'dika mastata'tu, a'udhu bika min sharri ma sana'tu, abuw'u laka bidhanbi, wa abuw'u laka bini'matika 'alayya faghfirli, fa innahu la yaghfirudh-dhunuba illa anta (O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You have created me and I am Your slave and I am keeping my promise and covenant to You as much as I can. I seek refuge with You from the evil of what I do. I acknowledge Your blessing and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for there is none who can forgive sin except You.)' If he says this in the morning, believing in it firmly, and dies on that day before evening comes, he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening, believing firmly in it, and dies before morning comes, he will enter Paradise."" Al-Walid bin Tha'labah contradicted him. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5522)"
"933","The Prophet [SAW] said: ""The best of prayers for forgiveness is for a person to say: 'Allahumma, anta rabbi, la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduka, wa ana 'ala 'ahdika wa wa'dika mastata'tu, a'udhu bika min sharri ma sana'tu, abuw'u laka bidhanbi, wa abuw'u laka bini'matika 'alayya faghfirli, fa innahu la yaghfirudh-dhunuba illa anta (O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You have created me and I am Your slave and I am keeping my promise and covenant to You as much as I can. I seek refuge with You from the evil of what I do. I acknowledge Your blessing and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for there is none who can forgive sin except You.)' If he says this in the morning, believing in it firmly, and dies on that day before evening comes, he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening, believing firmly in it, and dies before morning comes, he will enter Paradise."" Al-Walid bin Tha'labah contradicted him. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5522)"
"934","I will order a wasq of dates to be given to you, and if you wish, I will teach you some words which will be better for you. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Teach me those words and also order a wasq to be given to me. I am in dire need of it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Recite this: ""O Allah! When I am sitting, protect me regarding Islam, and when I am standing, protect me regarding Islam, and when I am sleeping, protect me regarding Islam, and do not accept the word of any jealous enemy about me, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You have seized, and I ask You for goodness, all of which is in Your Hand of Power."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, Hashim bin Abdullah bin Zubair was 9 years old."
"935","The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) When people are amassing treasures of dinars and dirhams, you should amass the treasure of these words: ""O Allah! I ask You for steadfastness in religion, and I ask You for determination in guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, and I ask You for good worship of You, and I ask You for every good that You know, and I seek refuge in You from every evil that You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. Surely, You are the Knower of the unseen."
"936","Did you supplicate for anything or beg of Him about that? He said: Yes. I used to utter (these words): Impose punishment upon me earlier in this world, what Thou art going to impose upon me in the Hereafter. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Hallowed be Allah, you have neither the power nor forbearance to take upon yourself (the burden of His Punishment). Why did you not say this: O Allah, grant us good in the world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the torment of Fire. He (the Holy Prophet) made this supplication (for him) and he was all right. (Using translation from Muslim 2688a)"
"937",""" Our Lord, grant us the good in this world and the good in the Hereafter and save us from the torment of Hell Fire."" (Using translation from Muslim 2690b)"
"938","They said to Anas b. Malik: ""Pray to Allah for us."" He said: ""O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."" They said: ""Increase for us."" So he repeated it. They said: ""Increase for us."" So he repeated it. They said: ""Increase for us."" He said: ""What do you want? I asked for you the best of this world and the Hereafter."""""
"939","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to make this supplication) ""O Allah! Grant us goodness in this world and goodness in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of Hell."" The narrator states: I met Ismail and asked him about this, so he said: (The wording of the narration is) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would often make this supplication: ""Our Lord! Grant us goodness in this world and also goodness in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of Hell."
"940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) most frequently made this supplication: ""O Allah! O our Lord! Grant us good in this world, and grant us good in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of Hell."
"941","Did you supplicate for anything or beg of Him about that? He said: Yes. I used to utter (these words): Impose punishment upon me earlier in this world, what Thou art going to impose upon me in the Hereafter. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Hallowed be Allah, you have neither the power nor forbearance to take upon yourself (the burden of His Punishment). Why did you not say this: O Allah, grant us good in the world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the torment of Fire. He (the Holy Prophet) made this supplication (for him) and he was all right. (Using translation from Muslim 2688a)"
"942","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say, 'I believe in Allah,' and then remain steadfast upon it."
"943","""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'There is no heart that is not between two of the Fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills, He guides it and if He wills, He sends it astray.' The Messenger of Allah used to say: 'O You Who makes hearts steadfast make our hearts steadfast in adhering to Your religion.' And he said: 'The Scale is in the Hand of the Most Merciful; He will cause some peoples to rise and others to fall until the day of Resurrection.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 199)"
"944","The servant will say: O my Lord, how could I visit You, while You are the Lord of all the worlds? Allah Almighty will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant was ill, but you did not visit him? Did you not know that if you had visited him, you would have found its reward with Me? Then Allah Almighty will say: I asked you for water to drink, but you did not give Me water to drink. The servant will say: O my Lord, how could I give You something to drink, while You are the Lord of all the worlds? Allah Almighty will say: Did you not know, My such-and-such servant asked you for water, but you did not give him water? Did you not know that if you had given him water to drink, you would have found its reward with Me? O son of Adam, I asked you for food, but you did not give Me food. The servant will say: O my Lord, how could I feed You, while You are the Lord of all the worlds? Allah Almighty will say: Did you not know that My such-and-such servant asked you for food, but you did not give him food? If you had given him food, you would have found its reward with Me."
"945","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took that date out of my mouth along with the saliva and put it back among the dates. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to teach us this supplication: ""O Allah! Grant me guidance among those whom You have guided, and grant me well-being among those whom You have granted well-being, and become my guardian among those whom You have taken as guardians. Bless for me what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Surely, You decree and none can decree against You. The one whom You protect is never humiliated."" The narrator named Shu'bah says: I think these words are also in the narration: ""You are Blessed and Exalted."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Abu al-Jawza' is Rabi'ah bin Shayban Sa'di, and Abu al-Jawza's name is Aws bin Abdullah, and both of these gentlemen are Tabi'in and both are residents of Basra."
"946","Teach me the words which I should (often) utter. He said: Utter,"" There is no god but Allah, the One, having no partner with Him. Allah is the Greatest of the great and all praise is due to Him. Hallowed be Allah, the Lord of the worlds, there is no Might and Power but that of Allah, the All-Powerful and the Wise."" He (that desert Arab) said: These all (glorify) my Lord. But what about me? Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: You should say:"" O Allah, grant me pardon, have mercy upon me, direct me to righteousness and provide me sustenance."" Musa (one of the narrators) said: I think he also said:"" Grant me safety."" But I cannot say for certain whether he said this or not. Ibn Abi Shaiba has not made a mention of the words of Musa in his narration. (Using translation from Muslim 2696)"
"947","The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate Allah: ""My Lord, help me and do not give help against me; grant me victory, and do not grant victory over me; plan on my behalf and do not plan against me; guide me, and made my right guidance easy for me; grant me victory over those who act wrongfully towards me; O Allah, make me grateful to Thee, mindful of Thee, full of fear towards Thee, devoted to Thy obedience, humble before Thee, or penitent. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, clearly establish my evidence, guide my heart, make true my tongue and draw out malice in my breast."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1510)"
"948","The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate Allah: ""My Lord, help me and do not give help against me; grant me victory, and do not grant victory over me; plan on my behalf and do not plan against me; guide me, and made my right guidance easy for me; grant me victory over those who act wrongfully towards me; O Allah, make me grateful to Thee, mindful of Thee, full of fear towards Thee, devoted to Thy obedience, humble before Thee, or penitent. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, clearly establish my evidence, guide my heart, make true my tongue and draw out malice in my breast."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1510)"
"949","I heard the Prophet saying: ""O Allah! Make our well-being good in all matters and save us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter."" This narration is also transmitted with another chain. However, in that narration, instead of the word ""well-being"" (), the word ""end"" () with the letter ""qaf"" is mentioned."
"950","I heard Abu Bakr as-Siddeeq on this minbar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on this day last year-then Abu Bakr wept, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿYou will not be given anything, after the word of sincerity (i.e., the Shahadah), like well-being, so ask Allah for well-being.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 10)"
"951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Ask Allah Almighty for forgiveness and well-being."" He again inquired, ""What should I ask from Allah Almighty?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Ask Allah Almighty for forgiveness and well-being."
"952","I came to Madinah one year after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I found Abu Bakr addressing the people. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood before us last year... and he wept and struggled to speak three times, then he said: 0 people, ask Allah for well-being for no one is given, after certainty of faith, anything like well being and nothing worse than doubt after disbelief. You should be truthful, for it guides to righteousness and they lead to Paradise. Beware of lying, for it guides to immorality and they both lead to Hell. (Using translation from Aḥmad 44)"
"953","I seek blessing for you and perform ruqyah on you from every illness that harms you, and for protection from the envy of every envier, and for protection from the evil eye and poison. May Allah grant you healing."
"954","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Forgive my striving (or seriousness), my jest, my mistakes, my intentional actions, and everything that comes from me."
"955","""The Prophet ﷺ used to say: 'Allahumma tahhirni bith-thalji wal-barad wal-ma' al-barid, Allahumma tahhirni min adh-dhunub kama yutahhar ath-thawb al-abyad min ad-danas (O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water, O Allah, purify me of sin as a white garment is cleansed of dirt)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 403)"
"956","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! All praise is due to You, praise that fills the heavens and fills the earth and fills whatever else You will after that. Purify me with snow, hail, and cold water. O Allah! Cleanse me of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt."
"957",""" O Allah, forgive me my faults, my ignorance, my immoderation in my concerns. And Thou art better aware (of my affairs) than myself. O Allah, grant me forgiveness (of the faults which I committed) seriously or otherwise (and which I committed inadvertently and de- liberately. All these (failings) are in me. O Allah, grant me forgiveness from the fault which I did in haste or deferred, which I committed in privacy or in public and Thou art better aware of (them) than myself. Thou art the First and the Last and over all things Thou art Omnipotent."" (Using translation from Muslim 2719a)"
"958","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Harithah! Indeed, Paradise has many levels, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaus. When you ask Allah Almighty, then ask Him for (the Paradise of) Firdaus."
"959","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, ""O Allah, You have beautified my physical appearance, so beautify my character ˹as well˺."""""
"960","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Remove from me disliked manners, desires of the self, bad habits, and diseases."
"961","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never failed to utter these supplications in the evening and in the morning: O Allah, I ask Thee for security in this world and in the Hereafter: O Allah! I ask Thee for forgiveness and security in my religion and my worldly affairs, in my family and my property; O Allah! conceal my fault or faults (according to Uthman's version), and keep me safe from the things which I fear; O Allah! guard me in front of me and behind me, on my right hand and on my left, and from above me: and I seek in Thy greatness from receiving unexpected harm from below me."" AbuDawud said: Waki' said: That is to say, swallowing by the earth. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5074)"
"962","O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that I may say in the morning and in the evening and when I go to bed. He said: ʿSay: O Allah, Creator of the heavens and the earth. Knower of the unseen and the seen – or he said: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Creator of the heavens and the earth - Lord and Sovereign of all things, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self and the evil of the Shaitan and the shirk to which he calls people.” It was narrated that Ya'la bin ʿAta' said: I heard 'Amr bin 'Asim bin ‘Abdullah... a similar report. (Using translation from Aḥmad 51)"
"963","I ask You for the goodness of this day, the goodness within it, and the goodness that comes after it, and I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, an evil age, the trial of Dajjal, and the punishment of the grave.” (The narrator states:) When evening would come, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite similar words. Hasan bin Ubaidullah has narrated this from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) with his chain of narration. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would also recite in this supplication: “There is no deity except Allah, He is the One and Only, He has no partner. Sovereignty belongs exclusively to Him, all praise is exclusively for Him, and He has power over everything.”"
"964","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this in the morning: ""O Allah! With Your help we have reached the morning, with Your help we reach the evening, with Your help we live and with Your help we die, and to You is the return."
"965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite these words in the morning: ""O Allah! With Your help we enter the morning, with Your help we enter the evening, with Your help we live, with Your help we die, and to You is the return."
"966","when going to bed, the Prophet (saas) used to say: ""Allahumma Rabbas-samawati wa Rabbal-ardi, wa Rabba kulli shay'in, faliqal-habbi wan-nawa, munzilat-Tawrati wal-Injili wal-Qur'anil-'Azim. A'udhu bika min sharri kulli dabbatin Anta akhidhun binasiyatiha, Antal-Awwalu fa laysa qablaka shayun, wa Antal-Akhiru, fa laysa ba'daka shayun', Antaz-zahiru, fa laysa fawqaka shayun', wa antal-batinu fa laysa dunaka shay', aqdi 'annid-dayna waghnini minal-faqr (O Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth and Lord of all things, Cleaver of the seed and the kernel, Revealer of the Tawrah, the Injil and the Magnificent Qur'an, I seek refuge with You from the evil of every creature You seize by the forelock. You are the First and there is nothing before You; You are the Last and there is nothing after You; You are the Most High (Az-Zahir) and there is nothing above You, and You are the Most Near (Al-Batin) and there is nothing nearer than You. Settle my debt for me and spare me from poverty)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3873)"
"967","I beseech you by Allah and by the bond of kinship between us, that we are suffering from severe famine and are eating al-'ilhaz (i.e., hair and blood). So Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « » . (Al-Mu’minun: 76) ""And We seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves before their Lord, nor did they supplicate with humility."
"968","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: No one of you should wish for death for any calamity that befalls him, but he should say: O Allah! cause me to live so long as my life is better for me ; and cause me to die where death is better for me. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3108)"
"969","""None of you should wish for death because of some harm that befalls him, rather he should say: 'Allahumma ahini ma kanatil-hayatu khairanli wa tawaffani idha kanatil-wafatu khairanli (O Allah, keep me alive so alive so long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me.)""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1820)"
"970","I hope for Your mercy, so do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye, and set all my affairs right. There is no deity except You."
"971","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So one third of the mountain (i.e., the rock) moved from its place. The second person said: O Allah! If You know this, I had parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel. When I came to them, both were asleep. I stood waiting until they woke up, and then they drank it. If You know that I did this hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then remove this difficult situation from us. So (another) one third of the rock moved. The third person said: O Allah! You know this, one day I hired a man as a laborer. He worked for me for half a day. I gave him his wages, but he expressed displeasure and did not take it. So I started working further with that wage until it became a lot of wealth. That man came to receive his wage, so I said: Take all these things. If I wanted, I could have given him only his wage at that time. If You know that I did this hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then grant us relief. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So the rock moved away, and those people walked out. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The words of the narration ""so I did more for him"" mean that I did more for him, because the Arabs use the word ""ala"" in the meaning of ""lahu"" in their idiom. Saeed bin Abul Hasan heard hadith from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in Madinah Munawwarah, because he was raised there, and Hasan could not hear hadith from him because he left Madinah Munawwarah in his childhood."
"972","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) Then Allah Almighty will remove his grief and replace his sorrow with happiness."" The people said: ""O Messenger of Allah! It is appropriate for us that we should learn these words."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes, it is appropriate for everyone who hears them to learn them."
"973","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Allah! Forgive my people, for they do not know.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant by this is that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) made this supplication on the day of the Battle of Uhud, when his face was wounded. He said: “O Lord! Forgive my people.” That is, forgive them for the sin they committed by wounding my face. This does not mean that forgiveness was being sought for the disbelievers, because if at that time you had prayed for their forgiveness, they would have certainly become Muslim at that very moment."
"974","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:"",""*allāhumma lā sahlan illā mā jaʿaltahū sahlan"",""wa-anta tajʿal al-ḥazna sahlan idhā shiʾta*"",""*(O Allah"",""there is no ease except what You make easy"","" and You make the difficult easy if You Will.)*"""""
"975","""One of you is granted an answer (to his supplication) provided he does not say: 'I prayed but I was not granted an answer.'"" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1484)"
"976","The supplication of the servant is granted in case he does not supplicate for sin or for severing the ties of blood, or he does not become impatient. It was said: Messenger of Allah, what does:"" If he does not grow impatient"" imply? He said: That he should say like this: I supplicated and I supplicated but I did not find it being responded. and theu he becomes frustrated and abandons supplication. (Using translation from Muslim 2735c)"
"977","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""No person should say: O Allah! If You will, then help me! Because there is none who can compel Allah. A person should ask with full confidence."
"978","I should not find you in such a state that you come to the people while they are engaged in their own conversation, and then you interrupt their talk. It should be such that the people listen to you attentively, then you converse with them, and when supplicating, avoid using rhymed and artificial words, because I have seen the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his companions disliked this."
"979","The people of the Daus tribe are being disobedient and are not accepting (the call to Islam). Please supplicate to Allah against them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed: ""O Allah! Guide the Daus tribe and bring them into the fold of Islam."
"980","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, raised both his hands and supplicated: ""O Allah! Grant guidance to the tribe of Daws."
"981","I was supplicating, was the grave of (my mother) Amina bint Wahb. I asked my Lord for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but I was not granted permission. This verse was revealed to me: “It is not appropriate for the Prophet and the believers to seek forgiveness for the polytheists.” So the same feeling overcame me as a child has for his mother. This made me weep. Beware! I had forbidden you from visiting graves, but now you should visit them, for they make one disinterested in the world and inclined towards the Hereafter."
"982","My uncle, you just make a profession that there is no god but Allah, and I will bear testimony before Allah (of your being a believer), Abu Jahl and 'Abdullah b. Abi Umayya addressing him said: Abu Talib, would you abandon the religion of 'Abdul-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ constantly requested him (to accept his offer), and (on the other hand) was repeated the same statement (of Abu Jahl and 'Abdullah b. Abi Umayya) till Abu Talib gave his final decision and be stuck to the religion of 'Abdul-Muttalib and refused to profess that there is no god but Allah. Upon this the Messenger of Allah remarked: By Allah, I will persistently beg pardon for you till I am forbidden to do so (by God), It was then that Allah, the Magnificent and the Glorious, revealed this verse: "" It is not meet for the Prophet and for those who believe that they should beg pardon for the polytheists, even though they were their kith and kin, after it had been made known to them that they were the denizens of Hell"" (ix. 113) And it was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: "" Verily thou canst not guide to the right path whom thou lovest. And it is Allah Who guideth whom He will, and He knoweth best who are the guided"" (xxviii, 56). (Using translation from Muslim 24a)"
"983","Ibn ‘Abbas reported the Prophet ﷺ as saying “If anyone who means to have intercourse with his wife says “In the name of Allaah, O Allaah, keep us away from the devil and keep the devil away from what You hast provided us.” It will be ordained that no devil will ever harm the child born to them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2161)"
"984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will come to your place. I said to my wife: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will come to our place, so try to avoid talking to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) or causing him any discomfort. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came, and I slaughtered a goat that was present in my house for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Jabir! It seems you know that I like meat very much. Then, when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was about to leave, the wife of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Please supplicate for mercy for me and my husband. (The narrator states) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did so. Then Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said to that woman: Did I not tell you not to say anything (to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)? The woman replied: Should the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) come to our place and then leave without supplicating for mercy for us?"
"985","""A Bedouin entered the mosque when the Messenger of Allah was sitting there, and (the man) said: 'O Allah, forgive me and Muhammed, and do not forgive anyone else with us.' The Messenger of Allah smiled and said: 'You have placed restrictions on something that is vast.' Then the Bedouin turned away, went to a corner of the mosque, spread his legs and began to urinate. After he had a better understanding, the Bedouin said: 'He got up and came to me, and may my father and mother be ransomed for him, he did not rebuke me nor revile me. He said: ""This mosque is not for urinating in. Rather it is built for the remembrance of Allah and prayer.'"" Then he called for a large vessel of water and poured it over the place where he had urinated."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 529)"
"986","narrates: A man said: O Allah! Grant forgiveness only to me and Muhammad (peace be upon him). So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You have withheld (this forgiveness) from many people. (That is, you did not let it reach them.)"
"987","Abu Hurairah said; The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) got up for the prayer and we also stood up along with him. A Bedouin said said during prayer; O Allah, show mercy to me and to Muhammed and do not show mercy to anyone along with us. When the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) uttered the salutation, he said to the Bedouin; you narrowed down a vast (thing). By this he meant the mercy of Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 882)"
"988",": When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, he began with himself and said: May the mercy of Allah be upon us and upon Moses. If he had patience, he would have seen marvels from his Companion. But he said: ""(Moses) said: If ever I ask thee about anything after this, keep me not in they company: then wouldst thou have received (full) excuse from my side"". Hamzah lengthened it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3984)"
"989","There is no believing servant who supplicates for his brother behind his back (in his absence) that the Angels do not say: The same be for you too. (Using translation from Muslim 2732a)"
"990","I am fasting."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed voluntary prayer. We also prayed behind him in congregation. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called Lady Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) and the members of her household. Lady Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have a request."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm Sulaym! What is it?"" She said: ""Your servant Anas (please supplicate for him)."" (Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates:) So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated for me for goodness in this world and the Hereafter. (He supplicated:) ""O Allah! Grant him wealth and children, and bless him in them."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Among the people, I have the most children. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: My daughter Amina has informed me that, until Hajjaj became governor of Basra, one hundred and twenty of my descendants (children and grandchildren) had passed away."
"991","The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of the lack of rain, so he gave an order for a pulpit. It was then set up for him in the place of prayer. He fixed a day for the people on which they should come out. Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the rim of the sun appeared, sat down on the pulpit, and having pronounced the greatness of Allah and expressed His praise, he said: You have complained of drought in your homes, and of the delay in receiving rain at the beginning of its season. Allah has ordered you to supplicate Him has and promised that He will answer your prayer. Then he said: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe, the Compassionate, the Merciful, the Master of the Day of Judgment. There is no god but Allah Who does what He wishes. O Allah, Thou art Allah, there is no deity but Thou, the Rich, while we are the poor. Send down the rain upon us and make what Thou sendest down a strength and satisfaction for a time. He then raised his hands, and kept raising them till the whiteness under his armpits was visible. He then turned his back to the people and inverted or turned round his cloak while keeping his hands aloft. He then faced the people, descended and prayed two rak'ahs. Allah then produced a cloud, and the storm of thunder and lightning came on. Then the rain fell by Allah's permission, and before he reached his mosque streams were flowing. When he saw the speed with which the people were seeking shelter, he ﷺ laughed till his back teeth were visible. Then he said: I testify that Allah is Omnipotent and that I am Allah's servant and apostle. Abu Dawud said: This is a ghraib (rate) tradition, but its chain is sound. The people of Medina recite ""maliki"" (instead of maaliki) yawm al-din"" (the master of the Day of Judgement). But this tradition (in which the word maalik occurs) is an evidence for them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1173)"
"992","A man entered the masjid when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing and delivering the Khutbah. He turned to face the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, our wealth has been destroyed and the routes have been cut off. Pray to Allah (SWT) to send us rain.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands then said: ""O Allah, send us rain."" Anas said: ""By Allah, we had not seen even a wisp of a cloud in the sky and there were no houses or buildings between us and (the mountain of ) Sal'. Then a cloud like a shield appeared, and when it reached the middle of the sky it spread and it began to rain."" Anas said: ""By Allah, we did not see the sun for a week. Then a man entered through that door on the following Friday, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing and delivering the Khutbah. He turned to face him standing and said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, may Allah (SWT) send blessings upon you. Our wealth has been destroyed and the routes have been cut off. Pray to Allah (SWT) to withold (the rain) from us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and said: 'O Allah, around us and not on us.; O Allah, on the hills and mountains, the bottoms of the valleys and where the trees grow.' Then it stopped raining and we went out walking in the sun."" Sharik said: 'I asked Anas: 'Was he the same man?' He said: 'No.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1518)"
"993","“Allahumma aj’alhu sayyiban hani’an (O Allah, make it a wholesome rain cloud).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3890)"
"994","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saw clouds, he would supplicate: ""O Allah! Let it be heavy and beneficial."
"995","The famine would not break out because of drought, but there would be famine despite heavy rainfall as nothing would grow from the earth. (Using translation from Muslim 2904)"
"996","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to teach us the words of Tashahhud during prayer just as he used to teach us a surah from the Qur'an. Just as he used to teach us the words of Tashahhud, he also used to teach us to say these words: ""O Allah! Create affection between our hearts and reconcile our differences, and guide us to the paths of peace, and deliver us from darkness into light, and keep us away from outward and inward indecencies. O Allah! Protect our hearing, our sight, and our wives, and make us among those who are grateful for Your blessings, and those who praise You for them, and those who accept them, and perfect them for us."
"997","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Indeed, there is an effect of Satan and there is an effect of the angel. The effect of Satan is that he leads back towards evil and denies the truth, and the effect of the angel is that he leads back towards goodness and affirms the truth. So whoever finds this situation, let him praise Allah Almighty, and whoever finds the other situation, let him seek refuge from Satan.\"" Then he recit"
"998","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! I ask You for guidance and steadfastness."" (These are the"
"999","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us this supplication as he taught us the surah from the Qur'an. He would say: O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge from You from the trails of Al-Masihid-Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1542)"
"1000","I do. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Who were they? The man replied: They died upon shirk (polytheism). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""If I did not fear that you would stop burying (your dead), I would pray to Allah that He make you hear the punishment of the grave as I have heard it. Surely, this Ummah will be tested in their graves."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned towards us and said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell and the punishment of the grave, seek refuge with Allah from the apparent and hidden trials, and seek refuge with Allah from the trial of Dajjal."
"1001","Sayyidah Umm Khalid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrate: (She narrates) I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) seeking refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. (Musa bin Uqbah says) I have not heard anyone else, besides this woman, narrate that ""I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"1002","I heard him recite this supplication: “O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of the chest, an evil life, and (evil) death.”"
"1003","the Messenger of Allah (saas) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from poverty, insufficiency and humiliation, and from wronging (others) and being wronged.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3842)"
"1004","The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us these words as he used to teach us the Book (Qur'an): ""O Allah! seek refuge with You from miserliness, and seek refuge with You from cowardice, and seek refuge with You from being brought back to (senile) geriatric old age, and seek refuge with You from the affliction of the world and from the punishment in the Hereafter."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6390)"
"1005","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the crowing of a rooster, it has seen an angel, so ask Allah from His bounty at that time and turn towards Him with desire. And when you hear the braying of a donkey, it has seen a devil. At that time, seek refuge with Allah from its evil, that which it (the donkey) has seen (i.e., the devil)."
"1006","narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw dust in the sky (i.e., a storm) or wind, he would seek refuge with Allah from its evil. (But) when it rained, he would say: ""O Allah! Let it be heavy and beneficial."
"1007","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The wind comes from Allah's mercy. Salamah's version has: It is Allah's mercy; it (sometimes) brings blessing and (sometimes) brings punishment. So when you see it, do not revile it, but ask Allah for some of its good, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5097)"
"1008","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports as a marfu’ hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): When a strong wind would blow, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would say (i.e., he would supplicate): “O Allah! Let it be heavy (with rain or clouds), not barren.”"
"1009","""The Prophet [SAW] used to say in his supplication: 'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika minal-kasali, wal-harami, wal-jubni, wal-bukhli, wa fitnatid-dajjali, wa 'adhabil-qabr (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, cowardice, miserliness, the tribulation of the Dajjal and the torment of the grave.)"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5451)"
